known, but related to Northern Sami luopma. Possibly from luoda. Alternatively, according to Rahkonen (2017), possibly borrowed from dialectal Estonian loom (“riverbend”), originally in the sense \"bend, draught\"; the Estonian word may then derive from Baltic (compare Lithuanian lomà (“lowland, dep"}]}